\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces  Per-frame Bad1, raw against refined, for \emph  {every} scored frame of each split --- five backbones, all sequences, no selection. Points below the diagonal are improved frames. On held-out D7 half improve against $13\%$ worsened, and the worsened band hugs the diagonal while the improved mass extends far from it: the frame-level form of the count-versus-magnitude asymmetry behind $B^+/H^+$. Disparity \emph  {maps} are not shown --- the intervention is sub-pixel on disparities of about $8$\,px, so at an honest colour scale they are indistinguishable. }}{6}{}\protected@file@percent }
